  {
    "name": "Equation Scope and Current Implementation",
    "width": 1560,
    "height": 2100,
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "How the supplied equations relate to the current shear code",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 80,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 85,
        "kind": "round",
        "color": "E7F0FF"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Adopted: F, Eq. (1), trilinear envelope; F, Eq. (2), local fatigue degradation\nbond.m / bond_strength.m; the 0.75δm threshold is used in active_nodes.m\nThe code adds zero-count protection, nonnegative peaks and a residual-stress rule.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 230,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 150,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "E5F3E9"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Adapted principle: bond-stress integration in F, Eq. (10), and S, Eq. (10)\nReplace half-span coordinates with local coordinates on each anchor: Ti(x)=pf∫[x,Li]τi dξ\nS, Eqs. (9d) and (11), motivate two-sided slip compatibility and intersection strain continuity.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 460,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 170,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "E5F3E9"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Not directly implemented: F, Eq. (9b), analytical matrix; S, Eqs. (9a–c), analytical slip fields\nanchorage.m assembles bar/bond stiffness and uses fixed-point iteration with a Newton fallback.\nThe numerical system is not the paper matrix merely because both are written as matrix equations.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 710,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 170,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "FFE9CD"
      },
      {
        "id": "e",
        "text": "Not included: Ps/Pd from F, Eq. (11), and half-span Ls/Ld relations from F, Eq. (13)\nThese belong to the longitudinal flexural IC-debonding model; its P is not this model’s total load Q.\nThe current code does not calculate critical loads or half-span damage-zone lengths using these equations.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 960,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 170,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "FFE9CD"
      },
      {
        "id": "f",
        "text": "Not included: longitudinally strengthened beam deflection from F, Eq. (14)\nThe eccentric longitudinal-reinforcement bending expression does not transfer directly to vertical NSM shear.\nHere q is a vertical crack jump and w is crack opening; the paper’s deflection w is a different quantity.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 1210,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 170,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "FFE9CD"
      },
      {
        "id": "g",
        "text": "Adopted equilibrium idea: E, Eq. (1), V=Vc+Vs+Vef\nHere V=Vc+Vs+Vf, where Vf sums the actual NSM bar-force vertical components.\nE, Eq. (2), Vef,σ+Vef,τ, concerns the continuous ECC overlay and is not implemented for these NSM bars.",
        "x": 240,
        "y": 1460,
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 180,
        "kind": "box",
        "color": "E5F3E9"
